{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And this for Judah.</b> He placed Judah next to Reuben because both of them acknowledged the wrong that was in their hands, as it says: ״אֲשֶׁר חֲכָמִים יַגִּידוּ וְגוֹ׳ לָהֶם לְבַדָּם וְגוֹ׳ וְלֹא עָבַר זָר בְּתוֹכָם״ (Job 15); and further, our Sages explained that all forty years that Israel were in the wilderness, the bones of Judah were rolling about in the ark because of the ban he accepted upon himself, as it says: ״וְחָטָאתִי לְאָבִי כָּל הַיָּמִים״ (Genesis 44). Moses said: Who caused Reuben to confess? Judah, etc. (Sotah 7)." "<b>Hear, YHWH, the voice of Judah.</b> The prayer of David and Solomon and Asa because of the Cushites, and Jehoshaphat because of the Ammonites, and Hezekiah because of Sennacherib." "<b>And to His people You shall bring him.</b> To peace from the war." "<b>His hands contend for him.</b> They shall contend his contention and avenge his vengeance." "<b>And You shall be a help against his adversaries.</b> Concerning Jehoshaphat He prayed concerning the battle of Ramoth Gilead: ״וַיִּזְעַק יְהוֹשָׁט וַה׳ עֲזָרוֹ״ (II Chronicles 18). Another interpretation — <b>Hear, YHWH, the voice of Judah</b>: here He alluded to Simeon from within the blessings of Judah, and even when they divided the land of Israel, Simeon took from within the lot of Judah, as it says (Joshua 19): ״מֵחֵבֶל בְּנֵי יְהוּדָה נַחֲלַת בְּנֵי שִׁמְעוֹן״. (And why did He not set aside a blessing for him on his own? Because he had a grudge against him on account of what he did at Shittim — so it is written in the aggadah of Psalms.)"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:42.659279499Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}